Title: last train

[[rdg
Tone: Drama
Start: An estranged father arrives to return a borrowed book before his daughter leaves the country.
End: She misses her train deliberately, but makes him ask her to stay.
]]

[[character: June
Voice: Quick, guarded; uses logistics to avoid emotion.
Want: Leave without another argument.
Obstacle: Her father has brought the book her mother annotated.
]]

[[character: Arthur
Voice: Careful, indirect; repairs things instead of apologizing.
Want: Find a reason for June to stay another hour.
Obstacle: He cannot admit that he is lonely.
]]

INT. STATION CAFÉ — LAST TRAIN
